l patch modifies the comparison in `ParseLV4MeshBonesVertices` to use `mBoneVertices.size()` instead of `mPositions.size()`. The older version uses a different variable naming convention (`filePtr` instead of `mFilePtr`) and slightly different function signatures for parsing floats. To backport this change, we need to:\n- Replace `mesh.mPositions.size()` with `mesh.mBoneVertices.size()`.\n- Ensure all references to `mFilePtr` are updated to `filePtr`.\n- Update any float parsing functions to match the older version\'s API (e.g., `ParseLV4MeshFloat` instead of `ParseLV4MeshReal`).\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nLow - The change is localized to a single conditional block and involves only renaming variables and updating function calls. It does not introduce new dependencies or alter the overall logic of the function.\n\nD. Fixed Code:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/code/AssetLib/ASE/ASEParser.cpp b/code/AssetLib/ASE/ASEParser.cpp\nindex 21675da29c..badfcec76e 100644\n--- a/code/AssetLib/ASE/ASEParser.cpp\n+++ b/code/AssetLib/ASE/ASEParser.cpp\n@@ -1406,8 +1406,8 @@ void Parser::ParseLV4MeshBonesVertices(unsigned int iNumVertices, ASE::Mesh &mes\n             if (TokenMatch(filePtr, "MESH_BONE_VERTEX", 16)) {\n                 // read the vertex index\n                 unsigned int iIndex = strtoul10(filePtr, &filePtr);\n-                if (iIndex >= mesh.mPositions.size()) {\n-                    iIndex = (unsigned int)mesh.mPositions.size() - 1;\n+                if (iIndex >= mesh.mBoneVertices.size()) {\n+                    iIndex = (unsigned int)mesh.mBoneVertices.size() - 1;\n                     LogWarning("Bone vertex index is out of bounds. Using the largest valid "\n                                "bone vertex index instead");\n                 }\n``` \n\nThis backported patch ensures compatibility with the older version while preserving the functionality of the original fix.', 'request_token': 0, 'response_token': 0}]
